# Claude Code settings. Neither file is committed.
#
# The shared project-level settings.json used to be tracked, on the reasoning
# that a permissions allowlist is team config worth sharing. It is not worth
# what it costs here: app_location is "/" on all four workflows, so the repo
# root IS the deployed site, and staticwebapp.config.json only gates /, /*.html
# and /api/*. Verified against production -- GET /.claude/settings.json
# returned 200 with the file's contents, unauthenticated, on both instances.
#
# The contents are not credentials, but they do list internal paths, resource
# group and database names, and the shape of our tooling. None of that belongs
# on a public URL.
.claude/

# Vendor API documentation. Kept locally, never committed: the root of this
# repo is served by the Static Web App, and staticwebapp.config.json gates
# only /, /*.html and /api/* behind authentication -- a real file at the root
# with no matching route would be publicly fetchable.
VNDLY API Docs.pdf
*.pdf
